{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Confusion Matrix.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Confusion Matrix.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"confusion matrix confusion matrix","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Confusion Matrix.md","fileName":"Confusion Matrix.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Confusion Matrix","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 22:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Social Content Popularity Prediction]] · [[Classification Evaluation and Visualization]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Social Content Popularity Prediction","Classification Evaluation and Visualization","bigdataincomplexandsocialnetworks.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Confusion Matrix.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Confusion Matrix.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"confusion matrix confusion matrix","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Confusion Matrix.md","fileName":"Confusion Matrix.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Confusion Matrix","heading":"Confusion Matrix","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A confusion matrix counts how often each actual class is assigned to each predicted class. For a chosen positive class, its cells yield true positives, false positives, false negatives, and true negatives.\n\nThose counts support accuracy, precision, recall, specificity, and F-measure. Inspecting the matrix is especially important when one class is rare because a high overall accuracy can conceal failure to identify that class.\n\nThe book derives held-out counts from predicted and observed classes, then uses them to interpret precision, recall, and the F-measure. Keeping the chosen positive class explicit prevents the same table from being read in contradictory ways.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Social Content Popularity Prediction","Cl